From abc8c97dab44609e9d4e06aeab50f0099d0fb8b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:47:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Material: arrays of the integration points in the memory of
 MFEM

The arrays of a material (gradients, thermodynamic forces, internal state
variables and energies of both states, blocks of the tangent operator)
are `mfem::Vector`s held by the new class `MaterialArrays`, a private
base of `Material` declared before the material data manager of MGIS,
which uses them without copy (initializer, `HOST` location, point by
point layout).

MFEM keeps track of the valid copies of each array (host, device); MGIS
writes through raw pointers. `MaterialArrays::synchronizeOnHost` copies
the arrays back to the host if needed and invalidates the copies on the
device, before an access by MGIS on the host. The deformation gradients
are initialized to the identity, as MGIS does for the arrays it
allocates.

MaterialArraysTest: sizes, use without copy by MGIS, identity of the
deformation gradients, values written on the device seen by MGIS and
values written by MGIS seen on the device, with the cpu, debug and cuda
devices (fails on the debug and cuda devices if `synchronizeOnHost` does
nothing).
